// @trap memory access out of bounds
// THE BOUNDS POLICY, STATED. VL adds no bounds check of its own to a linear-memory
// access: the engine's own check is the policy, and it traps loudly. webcraft's
// requirement says "engine memory trap or explicit check, either is fine", and a
// desync-class bug should be loud rather than recoverable — so this is the
// direction, not an accident.
//
// The access below starts at 65534 and is four bytes wide, so it runs two bytes
// past the end of the one page the module starts with. `load-page-boundary.vl`
// reads the last LEGAL address of every width; this is the one byte further.
//
// Note the reason text: a linear-memory fault reports as "memory access out of
// bounds", not as an array error. (It used to be relabelled — see `trapReason`
// in `tests/support/runWasm.ts`.)
print(__load_i32__(65534))
